// The TrueType bytecode interpreter of FreeType 2.14.3 (truetype/ttinterp.c)
// in its default mode for this build: interpreter version 40 ("minimal
// subpixel hinting", TT_SUPPORT_SUBPIXEL_HINTING_MINIMAL) with backward
// compatibility, render mode normal, not pedantic, no variation blend
// (GETVARIATION and GETDATA are unknown opcodes, GETINFO's bit 10 is clear).
//
// Every instruction follows its Ins_* function step for step, with FreeType's
// fixed-point helpers (font::fixed) and wrapping 64-bit adds, because the
// hinted outline is the observable: the same bits or nothing. FreeType's
// non-pedantic error behavior is kept: a bad reference does nothing (or
// pushes 0), a stack underflow reads zeros, and an error stops the program
// where it happened, leaving the points as they are.
//
// Shape differences: zones are two `Zone`s (0 = twilight, 1 = the glyph) and
// zp0/zp1/zp2 are indices; the glyph zone's lists are lent by the glyph
// loader (moved in for a run, moved back after). The round/move/project
// function pointers are small enums. Code ranges are offsets into the font
// file (the glyph's instructions are read in place, not copied).

module ultragui::font::tt_interp;

import {List, filled} from akikit::containers::list;
import {FontError} from ultragui::font::sfnt;
import {Vec26, kTagOn, kTagTouchBoth, kTagTouchX, kTagTouchY} from ultragui::font::outline;
import {
  div_fix, dot_fix14, mul_div, mul_div_no_round, mul_fix, mul_fix14, pad_round, pix_ceil, pix_floor, pix_round,
  vector_length, vector_norm_len,
} from ultragui::font::fixed;

